# Runtime environment reference. This file is not automatically loaded.
# Optional absolute data directory; default is the OS-local AtrisShare folder.
# PowerShell example: $env:ATRIS_SHARE_DATA_DIR = 'D:\AtrisShareData'
# ATRIS_SHARE_DATA_DIR=
# The desktop generates its own session token and binds 127.0.0.1 on a random port.
# Do not hard-code runtime tokens or change the bind address.
# Optional Google Desktop OAuth application configuration (see docs/YOUTUBE.md).
# ATRIS_SHARE_YOUTUBE_CLIENT_ID=<desktop-client-id>.apps.googleusercontent.com
# ATRIS_SHARE_YOUTUBE_CLIENT_SECRET=<desktop-client-secret-if-required>
# This is launch-environment configuration, not an account token input.
# Never put real configuration values, account tokens or passwords in this file.
